Sec. 1 (RCW 9.41.070): (2)(h) Has not provided proof that he or she has completed, or is statutorily exempt from completing, a recognized firearms safety training program within the last five years as provided in subsection (3) of this section.
Sec. 1 (RCW 9.41.070): (3)(a) A person applying for a concealed pistol license must provide proof that he or she has completed a recognized firearms safety training program within the last five years that, at a minimum, includes eight hours of instruction on:
Sec. 1 (RCW 9.41.070): (i) Basic firearms safety rules;
Sec. 1 (RCW 9.41.070): (ii) Firearms and children, including safe storage of firearms and talking to children about firearms safety;
Sec. 1 (RCW 9.41.070): (iii) Firearms and suicide prevention;
Sec. 1 (RCW 9.41.070): (iv) Safe storage of firearms to prevent unauthorized access and use;
Sec. 1 (RCW 9.41.070): (v) Safe handling of firearms;
Sec. 1 (RCW 9.41.070): (vi) State and federal firearms laws, including prohibited firearms transfers;
Sec. 1 (RCW 9.41.070): (vii) State laws pertaining to the use of deadly force for self-defense;
Sec. 1 (RCW 9.41.070): (ix) Live-fire shooting exercises on a firing range that include a demonstration by the applicant of the safe handling of, and shooting proficiency with, a pistol.
Sec. 1 (RCW 9.41.070): (c) The firearms safety training requirement of this subsection shall not apply to:
Sec. 1 (RCW 9.41.070): (i) An applicant who is a peace officer certified in accordance with RCW  43.101.095(1);
NEW SECTION Sec. 2 (effective date): This act takes effect January 1, 2021.
